Welcome to OOFEM Input manual README.

What is here
------------
The input manual: the structure and format of the OOFEM text input file, every
record and every attribute, with worked examples.

The reference is split by record group under ``pages/``.  ``quickstart.rst``
walks through a complete working input file record by record and is the place
to start reading; ``introduction.rst`` defines the notation the reference uses.

Prerequisities
----------------
To build the documentation, you need Sphinx (Python documentation generator,
https://www.sphinx-doc.org) and the MyST parser, which this manual uses for its
Markdown pages::

    pip install -U sphinx myst-parser

Building the PDF additionally needs a LaTeX installation; see doc/README for
the list of packages.

Building documentation
----------------------
1) Change working directory to doc/oofemInput inside your oofem source tree
2) run ``make html`` to build the html version, in ``_build/html``
3) for the pdf version run ``make latex``, then ``make all-pdf`` in
   ``_build/latex``

If a change does not seem to take effect, run ``make clean`` first: the build
reuses the parsed documents cached in ``_build/doctrees``.

Writing a record
----------------
A record is documented with the ``record`` directive from
``doc/_ext/oofemroles.py``, followed by a parameter list::

    .. record::

       :descitem:`StaticStructural` :elemparam:`nsteps{in}`
       :optelemparam:`deltat{rn}`

    **Parameters**

    :param:`nsteps{in}`
        Number of solution steps.

    :optparam:`deltat{rn}`
        Length of the time step.  Default ``1.0``.

``:descitem:`` is the record keyword, ``:elemparam:`` a mandatory attribute and
``:optelemparam:`` an optional one, which renders bracketed.  The type goes in
braces after the name.  Use ``:param:``/``:optparam:`` for the same attribute
mentioned in running text, where it renders with the same light background a
plain ``literal`` gets.

The directive takes an optional caption, which replaces the default "Record
syntax"; pass ``none`` to leave the block uncaptioned.

Keep the keyword spelling the one the solver actually registers, which is not
always the class name -- ``incrlinearstatic`` rather than
``IncrementalLinearStatic``.  The authority is the ``_IFT_<Class>_Name`` define
in the corresponding header.

Shared configuration
--------------------
Project metadata and the shared html settings come from ``doc/global_conf.py``,
and the page width, figure sizing and record styling from
``doc/_static/oofem.css``.  Do not set these per manual; see section [4] of
doc/README.

Happy contributing!
